# App bar — use FlowScreenAppBar

For any screen that shows a top bar with a title (and usually a back button), use **`FlowScreenAppBar`** from:

`lib/shared/presentation/widgets/navigation/app_bar_widget.dart`

Do **not** add custom `_FooAppBar` widgets, raw `AppBar(...)`, `CustomerFlowHeader`, or `CustomerSubscreenHeader`.

## Standard (back + title)

```dart
import '../../../../shared/presentation/widgets/navigation/app_bar_widget.dart';

Scaffold(
  appBar: FlowScreenAppBar(title: context.l10n.myScreenTitle),
  ...
);
```

## Customer profile sub-screens (pop or home)

```dart
appBar: FlowScreenAppBar(
  title: l10n.customerSavedAddresses,
  fallbackRoute: AppRoutes.customerHome,
),
```

## No back button (setup / confirmation / driver home)

```dart
appBar: FlowScreenAppBar(
  title: l10n.profileSetupTitle,
  showBack: false,
),
```

## Right-side icon(s)

```dart
appBar: FlowScreenAppBar(
  title: context.l10n.notificationsTitle,
  actions: [
    AppBarAction(icon: Icons.done_all_rounded, onTap: _markAllRead),
  ],
),
```

Or a custom widget via `trailing:`.

## Exceptions

Use **`AppBarWidget`** only when you need Material `AppBar` features not on `FlowScreenAppBar`: `AppBarLeadingType.menu`, centered title, `subtitle`, or `bottom` (e.g. `TabBar`).
